.TH SKOGAI-MODULE-TEST 1  "skogai-module-test 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
skogai\-module\-test \- run modules' tests with bats: core's contract, then the module's own tests/
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskogai module test\fR [OPTIONS] [MODULE]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.br
run modules' tests with bats: core's contract, then the module's own tests/
.br

.br
the contract (core's tests/contract.bats) runs for every module; its own
.br
tests/*.bats load core's tests/helper.bash for an isolated repo and layers.
.br
tests, and core's contract and helper, come from the source when there is one, else where it is found.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\fR=\fIFILTER\fR
.br
only tests whose name matches this regex
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.br
Print help
.TP
[\fIMODULE\fR]...
.br
default every module found
.SH "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES:"
.TP
\fISKOGAI_SYSTEM_DIR\fR [default: /etc/skogai]
.br
dir of the system layer config
.TP
\fISKOGAI_CONFIG_DIR\fR
.br
dir of the global layer, default ~/.config/skogai
.TP
\fISKOGAI_LOCAL_DIR\fR [default: .skogai]
.br
dir of the local layer; relative is from the git root, or pwd
.TP
\fISKOGAI_MODULE_PATH\fR
.br
colon\-separated dirs of module sources, default the one this module sits in
